"subs": [
{
"t": 4.3,
"dur": 2.268,
"text": "Hurry up and eat, Bin. Mom's live."
},
{
"t": 6.818,
"dur": 3.208,
"text": "Keep rushing him. He could chew all day… you still won't hear a thing."
},
{
"t": 10.826,
"dur": 5.58,
"text": "Back again, huh? Today's guest hides people for a living. First loss in eight hundred years."
},
{
"t": 16.656,
"dur": 1.699,
"text": "And it still doesn't know who beat it."
},
{
"t": 18.855,
"dur": 5.05,
"text": "I'm a ma giau — a hiding ghost. I hide people, mostly kids who won't quit playing."
},
{
"t": 24.156,
"dur": 6.899,
"text": "Simple rules. I hide them, their family looks. Bang the brass tray, call their name. One bang and I bring them back. That's a game."
},
{
"t": 31.304,
"dur": 8.642,
"text": "There's a deadline, too. The family has to look before dawn on day four. If nobody comes, the kid walks home, and eight hundred years at my job… becomes a joke."
},
{
"t": 40.195,
"dur": 4.896,
"text": "Eight hundred years without a single miss. Then apartment two seven zero eight."
},
{
"t": 45.592,
"dur": 5.714,
"text": "Dad's on a video call. Mom's livestreaming. The kid's gaming. Three people, three screens, one couch."
},
{
"t": 51.556,
"dur": 4.915,
"text": "Feng shui brass tray! One bang brings good fortune! Just three left! Sold!"
},
{
"t": 56.721,
"dur": 6.282,
"text": "Friday night, Bin skips homework to game in the stairwell. I shut the door and hide him from the whole family. Easy."
},
{
"t": 63.503,
"dur": 2.068,
"text": "I waited for the tray. Nine. Ten. Midnight."
},
{
"t": 65.82,
"dur": 4.071,
"text": "No one banged. Dad thought Bin was with Mom. Mom thought Bin was with Dad."
},
{
"t": 70.142,
"dur": 3.241,
"text": "You skipping homework too, mister? Can you get our Wi-Fi out here?"
},
{
"t": 73.632,
"dur": 2.061,
"text": "Eight hundred years, and nobody's asked me that."
},
{
"t": 76.194,
"dur": 10.634,
"text": "Day two, Bin ordered milk tea, with a note: leave it by the stairwell door on floor twenty-seven. He borrowed power from a maintenance outlet. Called this place his secret base."
},
{
"t": 87.077,
"dur": 1.783,
"text": "Am I a hiding ghost or a babysitter?"
},
{
"t": 89.36,
"dur": 7.87,
"text": "I made a Bin out of plant-pot dirt and sent him to the couch. Two little seed eyes. Obviously fake. His family would spot him and go looking."
},
{
"t": 97.481,
"dur": 7.045,
"text": "By day three, the mud kid had finished a whole week's homework. No arguing. No phone requests. Good as a statue."
},
{
"t": 104.776,
"dur": 3.729,
"text": "Our kid's so responsible, everyone! Secret's in the link below."
},
{
"t": 108.755,
"dur": 3.337,
"text": "His family noticed, all right. They noticed… this kid behaved better."
},
{
"t": 112.691,
"dur": 3.962,
"text": "Dinner on day three. The mud kid sat in the right seat, holding the right tablet."
},
{
"t": 116.903,
"dur": 1.665,
"text": "Four people. Three chewing sounds."
},
{
"t": 121.318,
"dur": 2.539,
"text": "Bin's so good today. Hasn't asked for a thing."
},
{
"t": 124.106,
"dur": 2.072,
"text": "Yeah. I'm gonna turn my camera off."
},
{
"t": 126.428,
"dur": 3.549,
"text": "I stood out on the balcony. For the first time in my life… I was scared."
},
{
"t": 131.977,
"dur": 4.119,
"text": "I'm out of milk tea. I'll go home in the morning. Did my mom ask about me?"
},
{
"t": 136.346,
"dur": 2.045,
"text": "I didn't answer. I hide people. I don't lie."
},
{
"t": 139.19,
"dur": 4.575,
"text": "Two a.m. Three hours till dawn. If this family won't bang the tray, I'll make them."
},
{
"t": 144.015,
"dur": 1.599,
"text": "I cut the power to the whole floor."
},
{
"t": 146.115,
"dur": 2.576,
"text": "Then I banged on the stairwell door. Bang. Bang. Bang."
},
{
"t": 148.942,
"dur": 8.874,
"text": "Mom thought a thief was stealing her stock. She grabbed the nearest thing on the shelf: the feng shui brass tray. And slammed it into the stairwell door."
},
{
"t": 158.065,
"dur": 1.931,
"text": "Where's Bin? Get Mom the flashlight!"
},
{
"t": 160.246,
"dur": 6.196,
"text": "She called his name to make him fetch a flashlight. The rules don't ask why. Tray bang, name called. I return him."
},
{
"t": 166.692,
"dur": 1.466,
"text": "Mom… were you looking for me?"
},
{
"t": 168.758,
"dur": 5.294,
"text": "By morning, sunlight hit the couch. The mud kid crumbled into a pile of potting soil."
},
{
"t": 174.302,
"dur": 1.71,
"text": "What a shame. He was so good."
},
{
"t": 176.412,
"dur": 7.238,
"text": "The real Bin got two sentences into his three days at the secret base. Then everyone looked back down at their phones."
},
{
"t": 183.9,
"dur": 3.033,
"text": "The mud kid made the honor roll. I'm thinking of opening a school."
},
{
"t": 187.534,
"dur": 3.502,
"text": "At dinner tonight, count how many chewing sounds your family makes."
},
{
"t": 191.635,
"dur": 6.912,
"text": "Next time: an illegal sand dock in flood season, and a ma da — river ghost — stuck on shift for seven years."
},
{
"t": 198.797,
"dur": 5.875,
"text": "Hit subscribe. Or tomorrow, when your mom bangs the tray, the one who comes back might not be you."
}
],
